	"name": "A Day's Labor",
	"type": "feature",
	"img": "icons/environment/wilderness/terrain-river-road-gray.webp",
	"system": {
		"description": "<p>Honest labor hardly satisfies most adventurers, who prefer to use their influence or persuasion to gain themselves a night in an inn or an hour on a stage. But for the classic vagabond, holding your hat in your hand while asking honest folk if they have work that needs doing is the surest, and most honest, way to a hot meal and a safe place to rest your head. In exchange for 1 hour of labor doing repairs and tending animals you can secure a moderate lifestyle of good food and sleeping in sheltered haylofts away from the troubles and vices of a tavern or other place of ill repute.</p>",
